In the square just defined, the conditional law of column $b$ given $E$ is its $\lambda_Y$ law given $p$. Moreover, $$\label{eq:square-row-locality}
 \mathbb E_{\lambda_Z}[q(\mathbf z_b)\mid E,(y_i)_{i\in I}]
       =u(E_b,y_b).$$ In particular, the conditional law of $y_b$ given $E$ is $m_Y(\,dy\mid w)$; in a single $Z$-state, the conditional law of its slot-$b$ state given $e=\omega_Z$ is the same fibre law over its old slot-$b$ parameter.
